1994 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Urban emergency services in India are heavily impacted by traffic congestion\056 Ambulances often fail to reach patients within the critical \042Golden Hour\042 leading to preventable deaths\056\n\nNearly 30\045 of emergency deaths are linked to delays in reaching hospitals\054 highlighting the urgency for innovation\056 Unplanned urban growth\054 increasing vehicle density\054 and the lack of dedicated emergency lanes further intensify these delays\056\n\nIn many cases\054 ambulances are reduced to basic transport vehicles rather than fully functional emergency response units\056 This exposes a critical gap in the system\054 where both speed and quality of care during transit are compromised\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 1995 0 R
     /Pg 1978 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1995 0 obj
  << /K [ 1994 0 R ]
     /P 2060 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1978 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

