2030 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The ECO ambulance transitions from road to elevated transport using a telescopic lifting mechanism designed for smooth\054 secure attachment\056\015\n\nThe process involves\072\015\nConnection \204 Extending connectors to reach the elevated track\015\nAlignment \046 Lift \204 Precisely positioning and elevating the vehicle\056\nLocking Mechanism \204 Securing the ambulance onto the track for stable movement\015\n\nOnce engaged\054 the system operates using electromagnetic suspension \050EMS\051\054 allowing the ambulance to levitate slightly above the track\054 reducing friction and ensuring a smooth\054 high\055speed journey\056\015\n\nTo enhance performance and adaptability\054 the system integrates\072\015\n\200 Magnetic levitation for frictionless travel\015\n\200 Linear motors for controlled\054 high\055speed propulsion\015\n\200 T\055rotation mechanism for seamless lane switching\015\n\nTogether\054 these innovations create a fast\054 stable\054 and adaptive transport system optimised for emergency response in complex urban environments\056)
     /K [ 26 ]
     /P 2031 0 R
     /Pg 1978 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

